React runs in the browser (client side), not inside the Docker container.
Docker only serves the built static files (dist/) to the browser.
Once the browser downloads them, all fetch() calls run on the user's machine — outside Docker.

So the browser cannot reach the backend port 8000 directly because it is never exposed.
Nginx acts as the bridge — browser hits port 80, Nginx proxies API calls internally to port 8000.
Port 8000 stays private inside the container, never visible to the outside world.


Client (browser) (REACT)
      │
      │  POST /shorten        → Nginx proxies → backend :8000
      │  GET /analytics/abc   → Nginx proxies → backend :8000
      │  GET /abc123          → Nginx proxies → backend :8000 (redirect)
      │  GET /                → Nginx serves dist/index.html
      ▼
   Port 80 (only public port)

